		<title type="html"><![CDATA[J's Job Jar for the iPhone/iPod Touch uses Bullet]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=17818#p17818"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br><br>I just received the approval notice for J's Job Jar, an iPhone app that simulates a glass jar filled with slips of paper with job descriptions written on them.  You can turn the phone upside down, move it around, shake it, etc., and the slips of paper bounce about in response.<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=445" class="postimage" alt="Paper slips flying about" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=446" class="postimage" alt="A job selected at random by shaking the jar." onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><br>Bullet adds a realism to the simulation that I could not have provided otherwise.  As an independent app developer I want to thank the entire Bullet community for providing such a valuable resoure.<br><br>-James Norton<br><a href="http://www.indiejames.com" class="postlink">http://www.indiejames.com</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5953">jnorton</a> — Tue Mar 09, 2010 10:56 pm</p><hr />
